  ('9830fd9b-dd19-53bc-bd91-d12135d78239', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$At the harvest party, Mrs. Adeyemi calls Mr. Halvorsen "the garden's backbone." What does she mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"His steady hard work gave the project the strength to hold together.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He has a very strong back that lets him lift heavy bags of soil.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"He was too proud and needed to be reminded to share the credit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He was the person who first came up with the idea for the garden.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His steady hard work gave the project the strength to hold together.$q$, $q$A backbone supports a body, so the metaphor means Mr. Halvorsen's effort, like refusing to stop "until every rock was gone," supported the whole garden. The idea for the garden came from Mrs. Adeyemi's meeting, not from him.$q$, 'draft', 'fcdfaa01-2c15-5899-b5f6-d27183a93eb3')
