   $q$In paragraph 2, young worker bees "act as nurses." What does this comparison mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They build new cells out of soft wax.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-roles"},{"text":"They fly out to gather nectar and pollen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-roles"},{"text":"They work in a hospital near the beehive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They take care of and feed the young bees.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They take care of and feed the young bees.$q$, $q$The sentence explains that these bees are "feeding the developing larvae," which is caring for the young like a nurse. Gathering nectar is the job of the foragers, not the young workers.$q$, 'draft', '8cafda76-e587-5302-bd0a-4cd85cba334e')
