  ('2907b14b-3694-5484-a8ad-4be696bb727d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author says the queen is "often misunderstood" because "Her title suggests that she rules the hive." What does this show about the word "queen"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The word suggests power and command, which does not match her real job.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The word is used only by scientists and is unknown to most readers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The word suggests weakness, even though she controls the colony.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-connotation"},{"text":"The word means a bee that lays eggs, so people use it correctly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The word suggests power and command, which does not match her real job.$q$, $q$"Queen" carries a feeling of ruling, but the author says "she does not give commands" and mainly lays eggs, so the word's associations mislead people. The idea that she controls the colony is exactly the misunderstanding the author corrects.$q$, 'draft', '8cafda76-e587-5302-bd0a-4cd85cba334e')
