   $q$In paragraph 1, Millbrook Creek is called "the town's forgotten backyard." What does this metaphor suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It was a private yard that belonged to one family in town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It was a nearby place that people ignored and did not care for.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It was the town's favorite park, visited by everyone daily.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It was a place so far away that nobody could find it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It was a nearby place that people ignored and did not care for.$q$, $q$A backyard is close to home, and "forgotten" matches the detail that "Most people drove past without a second glance." People drove right past it, so it was not too far away to find.$q$, 'draft', '756a1566-b585-55bb-ad40-7a1ea1811c87')
