   $q$The students found that the creek "was choking on trash and runoff." What does this personification show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The creek was flowing faster than usual because of the heavy rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-detail"},{"text":"The creek was making loud coughing sounds that people could hear.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Animals in the creek were getting sick from eating the students' lunches.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The trash and runoff were so heavy that the creek could not stay healthy.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The trash and runoff were so heavy that the creek could not stay healthy.$q$, $q$Choking means being unable to breathe, so the phrase shows the pollution was harming the creek badly. A creek cannot really cough; the phrase is figurative.$q$, 'draft', '756a1566-b585-55bb-ad40-7a1ea1811c87')
