   $q$The author says the cleanup "became a true odyssey." Based on the passage, what does this allusion mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The students read an old Greek story as part of their science class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The cleanup was finished in a single afternoon with no problems at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-allusion"},{"text":"The project was a long effort full of setbacks that took more time than planned.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The volunteers traveled across the ocean to reach the polluted creek.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The project was a long effort full of setbacks that took more time than planned.$q$, $q$The author compares the cleanup to Odysseus's "long journey" that was "full of delays and surprises," such as the storm and the four-month permit wait. A quick, problem-free cleanup is the opposite of what the allusion describes.$q$, 'draft', '756a1566-b585-55bb-ad40-7a1ea1811c87')
